<includeonly><onlyinclude><templatestyles src="PageBanner/styles.css" /><div class="page-banner" style="width: min(100%, {{#invoke:String|replace|{{{width|700px}}}|px}}px);">[[File:{{{1|BCWikiLogo.png}}}]]</div>{{#seo:
|image = {{{1|BCWikiLogo.png}}}
|description = {{{description|}}}
}}</onlyinclude></includeonly>
<!--KEEP THIS IN SYNC WITH [[Template:ResponsiveImage]]!!!-->
This template is used for images shown at the top of pages, such as gacha banners and event images. It also automatically includes the #seo parser function to set the page image and a description if provided. Another benefit of this template is that it is styled to shrink properly on devices with smaller widths so that the image does not overflow.

The proper shrinking effect can also be achieved using {{t|ResponsiveImage}}. If the image you want to scale is not at the top of the page above the lead paragraph, use ResponsiveImage.

==Usage==
<pre>{{PageBanner|File name|width=}}</pre>
The first parameter takes the name of the file to use as the page banner with the file extension included, and the <code>width</code> parameter is the maximum width of the image in px set to a default of 700px. No other values are necessary as the CSS preserves the image's aspect ratio.